{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/889179-compact-the-icelos-institute","id":889179,"title":"[Compact] The Icelos Institute","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-12T09:23:47-07:00","id":889179,"title":"[Compact] The Icelos Institute","content":"<i>Standing in the hall</i><br /> <i>Staring at the dark room</i><br /> <i>You know he\u2019s in there</i><br /> <i>But you can\u2019t move</i><br /> <i>Stuck in place</i><br /> <i>The mask looking out at you</i><br /> <i>Run damnit! Run!</i><br /> <i>He\u2019s coming</i><br /> <i>Face white eyes dripping red</i><br /> <i>Coming closer</i><br /> <i>Run! Have to run!</i><br /> <i>Feet nailed down</i><br /> <i>Wake up wake up wake up</i><br /> <br /> Is it any wonder people have bad dreams? Though it may seem hard to believe, nightmares exist to help us. They\u2019re a natural form of therapy, letting us process trauma without being in danger. It isn\u2019t always so simple though, nightmares recur when we struggle with our anxieties and disorders occur when our nightmares fail to function properly. Sometimes, especially in a world of darkness, they can even kill.<br /> <br /> Dr. Alice Calvert began her career in psychotherapy as a proponent of Jungian theory, analyzing archetypes of the collective unconscious and the power of symbols to the psyche. In particular she focused on \u201cNekyia,\u201d the dark journey, as a means to triumph over personal demons. Though seen as eccentric in her methods she gained a reputation for achieving breakthroughs in difficult cases.<br /> <br /> This would be put to the test when she was approached by Dr. Earl Wesley, a physician and sleep researcher confronted by an epidemic. Wesley ran a clinic out of an impoverished neighborhood whose residents complained of persistent recurring nightmares and insomnia. More frightening was the sharp rise in sudden deaths among those afflicted. These had been attributed to drug overdoses, suicides, and accidents from sleep deprivation but Wesley had begun to suspect a darker explanation, one hidden within the nightmares themselves. Desperate, he reached out to Dr. Calvert and allowed her free reign to explore her theories with his patients. Together they discovered a malevolent force guiding the dreams, the image of a porcelain face with bleeding eyes, stage directing their deepest terrors and preying on their self destruction. This wasn\u2019t a monster they could find or destroy, but they could teach its victims to fight back, to follow a Nekyia and take back their fear. In time they developed techniques for dealing with these extraordinary nightmares and pushing back against their influence on the waking world. The Icelos Institute was founded as a small network of clinics specializing in sleep medicine and psychotherapy with the goal of finding, diagnosing, and treating similar cases of extreme night terrors and fatal somnambulism.<br /> <br /> _____ <br /> <br /> Status 0 \u2013 You help out with the patients under the clinic\u2019s care and have training in providing for their special needs. You gain a free specialization in either Empathy or Science.<br /> <br /> Status 00 \u2013 You handle the physical infrastructure of the clinic, which frequently comes with heavy locks and reinforced glass. You gain a dot of Safe Place (Icelos Clinic).<br /> <br /> Status 000 \u2013 You are becoming more familiar with the Icelos method and have begun applying it in your own life. You gain either two dots of Meditative Mind or the Indomitable merit.<br /> <br /> Status 0000 \u2013 You have started undertaking your own Nekyia as well as guiding others through theirs. The labs where these occur are equipped to handle certain psychic phenomena. You gain the merit Mind of a Madman and an additional dot of Safe Place (Icelos Clinic).<br /> <br /> Status 00000 \u2013 Your Nekyia is complete. Nightmares no longer have power over you, you have power over nightmares. You have stolen the terror they once wielded and now it belongs to you. You gain up to three dots of a single Dread Power.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T10:18:13-07:00","id":889223,"title":"","content":"I like those guys. Are they an American or an European group? (I'm asking in order to determine where to put them in my &quot;map&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T19:28:03-07:00","id":889568,"title":"","content":"I envisioned them as being American. I'm going to try and finish the rest of the write up this weekend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T10:59:25-07:00","id":891249,"title":"","content":"The Enemy<br /> <br /> There is debate within the Icelos Institute about the source of these malevolent dreams. Some believe that the dreams are an internal phenomena, supernatural only in their fatality, with no outside cause beyond environmental factors. Supporting this idea is the lack of anything that can be identified as a unifying initiator, suggesting that the dreams are themselves the killer and the seeming presence of a sinister actor is the result of projection and personalization.<br /> Others view the disparity of the available evidence, while contradicting any single unifying cause, to be suggestive of multiple converging phenomena. The experiences of those afflicted, while widely divergent in some respects, tend to group into a small number of recognizable categories. Those that describe being stalked by creatures without human characteristics. Things heavy with mythological symbolism. Those that describe being watched by people with strange, alien features. Like a scientist with a lab rat or a director with his play actors. Those who feel they're being cursed or controlled by individuals they know. Abusers with an otherworldly power. Finally and most chillingly, there are those who are trapped in murderous narratives that repeat with growing urgency and danger. Urban legends and serial crimes that take on a life of their own.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Hunters<br /> <br /> You worked in a free clinic in a bad part of town. The little girl kept getting brought in with weird injuries. A lot of people thought it was her parents, but you saw the look in their eyes. The terrified, hopeless stare. You had an Icelos card in your wallet, and out of desperation you gave it to them. A few months later you got a call. The girl was fine now, better than she'd ever been. Also, would you be interested in a job?<br /> <br /> You were a PhD candidate researching the use of anti-seizure drugs to treat sleep paralysis. What you weren't expecting was to start suffering from sleep paralysis as well. The hallucinations were vivid. A demon squatting on your chest, telling you how you'd made it starve, chewing on you to sate its hunger. It got so bad you'd wake up with big black bruises. No matter how much you slept it stopped being restful. When you explained it to your adviser you were sure she'd think you were crazy. Instead, she had a solution in mind.<br /> <br /> You couldn't sleep more than an hour a night. The old man with the snakes appeared every time you closed your eyes. There was no escaping it. You were ready to give up. Icelos saved your life. Even more than the things they taught you, the tools they gave you to take back your dreams, just having someone hold your hand when you needed it meant the world. You're in it now one hundred percent. Patients like talking to you because you've been where they are. It's the least you can do to pay it forward.<br /> <br /> You were just an orderly. Patients tend to be under a lot of stress and are prone to violent outbursts even without things flying across the room on their own. Then you decided to try the Icelos method for yourself. Crazy as it sounds the hoodoo actually worked. You've got the sleep of reason. It lets you make do with less, which means longer shifts at the clinic making more money and helping more people. Its a win-win as far as you're concerned.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Methods<br /> <br /> Anesthetes believe that their first and foremost responsibility is to help victims. Their well being is paramount, keeping them alive, keeping them sane, letting them have a normal life again. Anything outside of that mission is a dangerous distraction that threatens to undo the good they've been able to do. These are people, sometimes even children, who have been through terrible trauma, and if they get lost in pursuit of some vendetta or crusade then you have failed.<br /> <br /> Phanerothymes are fascinated by the implication of their discoveries. The Icelos Method has the potential to be truly revolutionary, and pushing its limits can only be beneficial to those they are trying to protect. If dreams are not simply the processing of information in the sleeping brain then what else are they? What is the topography of the collective unconscious? Exploring the Nekyia and probing its deeper mysteries is their ultimate goal, even if some warn they are playing with fire.<br /> <br /> Phobetors don't think that they are doing enough. These dreams are symptoms of a more pernicious epidemic, one they have to take a more active role in combating. They seek out and track down the causes of fatal nightmares in the waking world, and eliminate them if they are able. This is the only way to make sure that the people they're helping stay safe, and if that means recruiting them into the hunt or even using them as bait that is a price that has to be payed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Stereotypes<br /> <br /> The Union \u2013 Some of our clinics, particularly in underserved areas, have had run ins with these groups. Call them neighborhood watches or home guards. They do what they can, but they tend to lash out at the first thing that presents itself, and when you can't see the thing preying on you that can get messy. We haven't always gotten along, locals can be paranoid about potential victims being locked up in weird labs, but communication is essential. They need our help more than most, and if we want to really make a difference we need them too.<br /> <br /> Null Mysteriis \u2013 We tend to run in some of the same circles so a passing acquaintance was probably inevitable. I wish I could say we worked better together. They don't like things that can't be measured, which tends to include dreams. A lot of them aren't big fans of Jungian theory either, they think its some outdated quackery. We've had plenty of debates about the rigor of our methodology, but when we have solid data to share with them I've never heard them say no. I'm hoping to collaborate with them on expanding our knowledge base.<br /> <br /> Loyalists of Thule \u2013 These guys might seem like strange partners but hear me out. Time was there was more than a little overlap in early psychology and the occult. Carl Jung had a lot of esoteric associates and disciples. A lot of their work has found its way into collections of the reformed Thule Society, along with plenty of other literature on hypnosis and dream study. Just don't tumble too far down the rabbit hole, you have to sort out the useful information from the mystical morass. They can be a bit eccentric, but we're on the same side.<br /> <br /> Cheiron Group \u2013 Yeah, I've heard of them. I'm pretty sure they got hold of one of our drug cocktails a while back, fast tracked it through the FDA, and started selling it. I'm not saying I disagree with them getting it out there, but that's a shady way to do business. There have been a couple of different companies trying to buy us out that I'm pretty sure are under their umbrella. What surprises me is why they haven't just forced the issue. I'm pretty sure if they could do it they would do it. One time I ended up on an email chain I wasn't supposed to and saw something about our name being a problem for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T12:45:14-07:00","id":891322,"title":"","content":"Certainly interesting, as well as an excellent way to bring Beast into Hunter or vise versa. Have a like!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T22:33:27-07:00","id":891590,"title":"","content":"So, I like this compact, but I find &quot;The Enemy&quot; section a little ambiguous. Is it basically saying that the Icelos Institute most generally tends to cross paths with Beasts, Changelings/Faeries, Avenger/Legend type Slashers, and &quot;Urban Legends&quot; (ghosts, spirits, and other unidentifiable horrors that bring urban legends to life)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T05:42:30-07:00","id":891678,"title":"","content":"That is precisely what it is saying, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}